@startuml power-domains
' LocalAiRobot — DETAILED power + signal wiring, TOP-TO-BOTTOM (one 3S LiPo -> ESC + UBEC/UPS to the Pi).
' This source lives next to its render. Regenerate in place (writes power-domains.png here):
'   plantuml -tpng docs/images/power-domains.puml
' No Graphviz needed: !pragma layout smetana. Vertical + larger fonts; Pi peripherals collapsed into one box.
!pragma layout smetana
top to bottom direction
hide stereotype
title LocalAiRobot — detailed power + signals (one 3S LiPo: ESC drive + UBEC -> UPS -> Pi; common ground)

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam TitleFontSize 22
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #333333
skinparam ArrowFontSize 15
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 12
  FontSize 18
  BorderThickness 1.5
  BackgroundColor<<io>> #DAE8FC
  BorderColor<<io>> #6C8EBF
  BackgroundColor<<model>> #FFF2CC
  BorderColor<<model>> #D6B656
  BackgroundColor<<data>> #D5E8D4
  BorderColor<<data>> #82B366
  BackgroundColor<<motor>> #F8CECC
  BorderColor<<motor>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<store>> #F5F5F5
  BorderColor<<store>> #666666
}

rectangle "3S 11.1V LiPo\n(single source)" as lipo <<motor>>
rectangle "ESC\n(battery input + BEC for servo)" as esc <<motor>>
rectangle "drive motor" as dmotor <<motor>>
rectangle "ZTW UBEC step-down\n3S in -> 5-6V / 6A out (jumper-set)" as ubec <<motor>>
rectangle "UPS HAT\n2x 18650 = backup buffer" as ups <<io>>
rectangle "Raspberry Pi 5\n+ Active Cooler (mandatory)" as pi <<io>>
rectangle "PCA9685\nI2C PWM bridge, 0x40" as pca <<model>>
rectangle "steering servo\nDS3225 HV (on the ESC BEC rail)" as servo <<motor>>
rectangle "Pi-powered peripherals\n(3.3V / CSI / USB-C from the Pi)\nHC-SR04P x3:  front 23/24 · left 5/6 · right 20/21\nCamera: Arducam IMX519 (16MP autofocus, CSI 22->15)\nFace screen:  USB-C -> /dev/ttyACM0" as periph <<data>>
rectangle "common GND bus\n(Pi <-> PCA9685 <-> ESC <-> UBEC)" as gnd <<store>>

' ---- power + signals, top -> bottom ----
lipo --> esc  : 11.1V (high current)
lipo --> ubec : 11.1V (tap)
esc  --> dmotor : motor drive
ubec --> ups  : 5-6V -> UPS input
ups  --> pi   : 5V to Pi
pi   --> pca  : 3.3V logic (VCC) + I2C SDA/SCL
esc  --> pca  : ch0 throttle PWM (signal)
esc  --> pca  : BEC -> V+ rail (servo power)
pca  --> servo : ch1: BEC V+ + PWM
pi   --> periph : 3.3V + TRIG/ECHO · CSI · USB-C

esc  ..> gnd : GND
pi   ..> gnd : GND
pca  ..> gnd : GND
ubec ..> gnd : GND

note bottom of gnd
  **ONE 3S LiPo powers everything** via two branches: the **ESC** (drive motor + BEC for the servo/V+ rail)
  and the **UBEC (5-6V) -> UPS input -> Pi**. The UPS 18650s stay as a **backup buffer** + clean shutdown.
  All parts share a **common GND**. The **ESC BEC -> PCA9685 V+ rail** is the servo's power (NOT the Pi's).
  **Servo: use an HV (7.4V) servo, or feed V+ from a separate 5-6V BEC** (a 6V-only servo can be damaged).
  Set the UBEC jumper to the UPS's rated input (typically 5V). DS3225 stall ~2.5-3A — if the ESC BEC browns
  out under hard steering, add a separate servo BEC on V+. All 3 HC-SR04**P** are 3.3V (ECHO Pi-safe).
end note
@enduml
